From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:16:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] build: link with the sanitizers, and no LTO when they
 trap

With -fsanitize-trap, a sanitizer's checks become trap instructions
instead of calls into its runtime; which form they take is decided
where GCC expands them. Under LTO that is the link, and lto-wrapper
passes no sanitizer option on from the objects: only the link line's
count. But many packages link with TARGET_LDFLAGS alone, as make's
built-in rule and meson do, and libtool drops -fsanitize-trap from
every link line. With CONFIG_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION holding
-fsanitize=undefined -fsanitize-trap=undefined, mtd, libnftnl and glib2
linked their checks as calls into libubsan, which the musl toolchain
does not have.

Add the sanitizer options of TARGET_CFLAGS to TARGET_LDFLAGS: a
sanitizer is a link option too, and a link that takes LDFLAGS then
expands the checks as traps, under LTO of the package's own making
(glib2's meson) too. And build without OpenWrt's LTO when TARGET_CFLAGS
asks for traps, so that the checks of a package that libtool links are
expanded where its objects are compiled. A build without sanitizers is
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 include/package.mk | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/package.mk b/include/package.mk
index f0e622a..97a6d48 100644
--- a/include/package.mk
+++ b/include/package.mk
@@ -54,11 +54,18 @@ ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,gc-sections,$(if $(CONFIG_USE_GC_SECTIONS),1,0)),1)
   TARGET_CXXFLAGS+= -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections
   TARGET_LDFLAGS+= -Wl,--gc-sections
 endif
+# Under LTO a sanitizer expands its checks at the link, with the link line's
+# options only, where -fsanitize-trap may be missing: expand them at compile time.
 ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,lto,$(if $(CONFIG_USE_LTO),1,0)),1)
+ifeq ($(filter -fsanitize-trap%,$(TARGET_CFLAGS)),)
   TARGET_CFLAGS+= -flto=1 -fno-fat-lto-objects
   TARGET_CXXFLAGS+= -flto=1 -fno-fat-lto-objects
   TARGET_LDFLAGS+= -flto=1 -fuse-linker-plugin
 endif
+endif
+# A sanitizer is a link option too: the link adds its runtime or, under LTO of
+# the package's own making, expands its checks as traps.
+TARGET_LDFLAGS+= $(filter -fsanitize%,$(TARGET_CFLAGS))
 ifdef CONFIG_USE_MOLD
   ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,mold,1),1)
     TARGET_LINKER:=mold
